JobScam Guard

An AI tool that helps students check job posts and recruiter messages for scam signs. Built for ForgeHacks 2026 (AI + Cybersecurity track).

Problem

Students and job seekers are targeted by fake job and internship offers (fake checks, fees, requests for personal data).

What it does
Recognize - a text classifier trained on fake job postings gives a scam probability.
Verify - rule checks look for red flags: payment requests, fake-check schemes, free email addresses, sender/company domain mismatch, moving to private chat apps.
Explain - plain-language reasons for the risk level.
Respond - next steps, reporting links, and a safe reply to send.
Results (baseline model, 20% held-out test set)
Class	Precision	Recall	F1
Fake	0.84	0.91	0.87

Confusion matrix: 157 fake caught, 16 missed, 31 real flagged as fake, 3372 real correct.

Limitations
Trained on an older public dataset; it may not generalize to short modern recruiter texts.
Some learned terms reflect dataset quirks, not scam behavior.
Rules can be avoided by a careful scammer. This tool is a helper, not a guarantee.
Tech

Python, scikit-learn (TF-IDF + Logistic Regression), rule-based checks, Streamlit. Optional LLM explanation via any OpenAI-compatible API.

Run it
pip install -r requirements.txt
streamlit run app.py
